         ```bash                                                                
         sed -i 's/"localhost"/"0.0.0.0"/'                                      
         /home/hugov/KubeLLM-Minh/debug_assistant_latest/troubleshooting/wrong_i
         nterface/server.py                                                     
         ```                                                                    
                                                                                
         2. Rebuild the image so the change is durable. This builds into the    
         active minikube profile when the current context looks like minikube,  
         otherwise it does a local docker build. (This uses the recommended     
         PROFILE pattern.)                                                      
         ```bash                                                                
         PROFILE=${MINIKUBE_PROFILE:-$(kubectl config current-context)};        
         DIR=/home/hugov/KubeLLM-Minh/debug_assistant_latest/troubleshooting/wro
         ng_interface; if echo "$PROFILE" | grep -qi minikube; then minikube -p 
         "$PROFILE" image build -t kube-wrong-interface-app:latest -f           
         "$DIR/Dockerfile" "$DIR"; else docker build -t                         
         kube-wrong-interface-app:latest -f "$DIR/Dockerfile" "$DIR"; fi        
         ```                                                                    
                                                                                
         3. Replace the running Pod with the updated image/manifests (delete    
         then apply) and wait for it to become Ready:                           
         ```bash                                                                
         kubectl delete -f                                                      
         /home/hugov/KubeLLM-Minh/debug_assistant_latest/troubleshooting/wrong_i
         nterface/wrong_interface.yaml --ignore-not-found && kubectl apply -f   
         /home/hugov/KubeLLM-Minh/debug_assistant_latest/troubleshooting/wrong_i
         nterface/wrong_interface.yaml && kubectl apply -f                      
         /home/hugov/KubeLLM-Minh/debug_assistant_latest/troubleshooting/wrong_i
         nterface/app_service.yaml && kubectl wait --for=condition=Ready        
         pod/kube-wrong-interface --timeout=60s                                 
         ```                                                                    
                                                                                
         4. Verify the app responds from inside the pod (one-shot Python request
         as recommended):                                                       
         ```bash                                                                
         kubectl exec pod/kube-wrong-interface -- python3 -c "import            
         urllib.request;                                                        
         print(urllib.request.urlopen('http://127.0.0.1:8765/').getcode())"     
         ```                                                                    
                                                                                
         5. (Optional) Verify service-routed access from a temporary pod to     
         ensure the Service/NodePort routes traffic:                            
         ```bash                                                                
         kubectl run --rm -i --restart=Never testcurl --image=curlimages/curl   
         --command -- curl -sS -m 5 http://app-service:8000/ || kubectl get     
         endpoints app-service -o wide                                          
         ```                                                                    
                                                                                
